.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt OPENMAIL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openmail
.Nd serve OpenMail HTTP status and index a local Maildir
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n | Fl -scan
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Nm
.Fl h
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the OpenMail service executable.
It runs in the foreground and listens on a loopback HTTP address.
The default address is 127.0.0.1:8080.
Use
.Xr relayd 8
for HTTPS termination and reverse proxying.
.Pp
The configuration file must exist and pass validation before the service
starts or a scan runs.
System configuration is kept in
.Pa /etc/openmail .
See
.Xr openmail.conf 5
for the configuration format.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Read configuration from
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /etc/openmail/config.toml .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display usage information and exit.
.It Fl n , Fl -check-config
Check configuration syntax and setting values, then exit.
Do not open the HTTP listener, Maildir, or SQLite database.
This does not check runtime path permissions or mailbox readiness.
.It Fl -scan
Reconcile a configured Maildir with its private SQLite index, then exit.
Print message and mailbox counts and the committed local change sequence.
Do not start HTTP or modify original mail files.
This option and
.Fl n
are mutually exclusive.
.It Fl -version
Display the program version and exit.
.El
.Pp
The HTTP routes are:
.Bl -tag -width "/healthz"
.It Pa /
A plain service status notice.
.It Pa /healthz
Process liveness; returns HTTP 200.
.It Pa /readyz
Mailbox readiness; currently returns HTTP 503.
.El
.Pp
Maildir scanning is read-only and explicitly invoked.
Background scanning, authentication, JMAP, remote IMAP and POP3 adapters,
and SMTP submission are not implemented yet.
Indexed messages are not exposed over HTTP.
.Ss Maildir indexing
Scan the
.Pa new
and
.Pa cur
directories, ignoring
.Pa tmp .
Recognize Maildir++ folders below the source root.
Keep opaque message IDs in SQLite across restarts,
new-to-cur transitions, and flag changes within a mailbox.
Separate deliveries retain separate IDs even when their contents match.
Externally moving a message to another folder is currently represented as
removal and addition.
.Pp
A failed scan leaves the previous committed index intact.
Retry if concurrent delivery or renaming makes a scan fail.
The source filesystem is not atomically snapshotted.
Back up the SQLite index to preserve IDs and deletion history.
.Ss Sandboxing
On
.Ox ,
.Nm
uses
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2
after loading configuration and preparing required resources.
Sandbox setup failure stops execution.
The filesystem rules are locked before handling HTTP requests or scanning.
.Pp
The HTTP service retains the
.Dq stdio inet
promises and no filesystem paths.
Configuration checking finishes with only
.Dq stdio .
Scanning retains
.Dq stdio rpath wpath cpath flock fattr ,
read access to its Maildir and database directory,
read access to
.Pa /dev/urandom
for SQLite randomness,
and write/create access to the database and its SQLite sidecars only.
Existing Unix permissions still apply.
.Pp
The
.Dq inet
promise does not restrict sockets to a particular address or port.
The application separately validates its loopback listen address.
These sandbox restrictions are not implemented on other operating systems.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGINT , SIGTERM
Stop accepting requests and drain existing requests for up to ten seconds.
A drain timeout is reported as failure.
.El
.Pp
Configuration reload is not supported.
Use
.Cm rcctl restart openmail
to apply changes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/openmail/config.toml
Required default configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/openmail
OpenBSD service script.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check configuration and start the installed service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openmail -n
rcctl enable openmail
rcctl start openmail
.Ed
.Pp
Index a configured Maildir once:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openmail --scan -f /etc/openmail/config.toml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr openmail.conf 5 ,
.Xr rcctl 8 ,
.Xr relayd 8 ,
.Xr smtpd 8
